    int quarterlySales[4] = {0}; // initialize all quarters to 0

    for (int i = 0; i < 12; ++i) {
        monthlySales[i] = getMonthlySales();

        // add sales to the corresponding quarter
        if(i<3) quarterlySales[0] += monthlySales[i];
        else if(i>=3 && i<6) quarterlySales[1] += monthlySales[i];
        else if(i>=6 && i<9) quarterlySales[2] += monthlySales[i];
        else quarterlySales[3] += monthlySales[i];
    }

    for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
        printf("Quarter %d sales: %d\n", i+1, quarterlySales[i]);
    }

    return 0;
}
```
This program first calls the `getMonthlySales()` function for each month of the year. It then adds up the monthly sales for each quarter and prints these sums. Note that we use the modulo operator (`%`) to ensure that the random number generated is between 0 and 100000. The `srand(time(NULL))` line seeds the random number generator with the current time, which ensures different output each time you run the program.
